# NX Redux: the app's N64 3D Resolution, live. GLideN64 draws at its 4:3 Resolution's window size (the app sets a
# multiple of 320 x 240; a wide aspect keeps its Wide Resolution's shape at that height): a new value mid-game resizes the
# window, which rebuilds GLideN64's frame buffers, and the geometry tells the frontend. ParaLLEl-RDP remakes its command
# processor between frames when its upscaling changes, and reports room for 8x from the start so a raise isn't cropped.
diff --git a/custom/GLideN64/mupenplus/Config_mupenplus.cpp b/custom/GLideN64/mupenplus/Config_mupenplus.cpp
